{
  "dom_id": "step-q132263",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Which of the following probabilities could be approximated using the normal approximation of the binomial distribution?\n\nI. The probability of a student getting $9$ correct answers on a test with $12$ questions if each question has $3$ options and the student answers all questions randomly.\n\nII. The probability of finding more than $50$ people with blue eyes in a randomly selected sample of $250$ if $40%$ of the population has blue eyes.\n\nIII. The probability that a biased coin lands on tails $35$ times out of $50$ coin flips if the probability that a single flip landing on tails is $0.6.$",
